"", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVeu8AEg", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 766, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8882916, "raw_content": "", "author": "TooTrick", "created": 1791830905303, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "OrangeManVryGood", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVeu8AEg.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/8TtGE1eSvskI.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/7O3k5us6AUwA0OJo.jpeg", "width": 768, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 639}], "blurhash": "UaLEKLVrt7xu_2IWWBoc_4xtt6Rj-=xut6WC", "full_resolution": [1665, 2000]}, "title": "Three of these have something in common. ", "last_comment_created": 1791844637348, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 22, "score_up": 766, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVewNJRs", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 13, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8884384, "raw_content": "\n800. 500. 450.\n \nThe numbers that would make your pellet rifle a federal \"firearm.\"\n\nA lot of kids learn to shoot with a pellet rifle, plinking cans in the backyard or keeping squirrels off the bird feeder, long before they ever carry a .22 into the woods. A California politician wants Congress to put that pellet rifle under federal gun control.\n\nThe bill is H.R. 10583, filed September 24th by Rep. Kevin Mullin (D-CA-15), and its title says it's written \"to classify lethal air guns as firearms.\" Once an air gun counts as a \"firearm\" under the federal Gun Control Act, buying one from a store means a federal background check, and the gun gets a serial number. The companies that make them and the stores that sell them need federal firearms licenses, and dealers keep federal paperwork on every sale.\n\n==\nWhat counts as a \"lethal air gun\"\n\n.177 caliber pellet\n800 feet per second or faster\n\n.22 caliber pellet\n500 feet per second or faster\n\n.25 caliber pellet\n450 feet per second or faster\n\nMetallic pellet above .25 caliber\nAny speed at all\n\nAnd then\nAny other air gun the Attorney General designates, through rulemaking, as \"capable of causing death\"\n==\n\nAny gun that can hit those numbers is a \"lethal air gun\" under the bill. The only ones carved out fire nothing but paint-filled pellets. That covers most serious pellet rifles sold today.\n\nNow look at that last line. The bill lets the Attorney General add more air guns through rulemaking, any he decides are \"capable of causing death,\" and it puts no limit on what that means. Today it's 800 feet per second. The bill already gives the Attorney General a blank check to decide which air guns come next.\n\nThe Red Ryder isn't on the list today. Daisy rates it at up to 350 feet per second, well under the line. But the bill lets the Attorney General add any air gun he deems \"capable of causing death.\"\n\nAdd your name to the North Carolina Firearms Coalition petition against H.R. 10583.\nhttps://action.ncfirearmscoalition.org/hr10583_pet?e=700b3d0d28cf25a534ef5a5f6eaf0d4b&utm_source=ncfc&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20261013_bbgun_rm2&n=3", "author": "theycallmedon", "created": 1791910493037, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "cyberrigger", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "They'd put your air rifle behind the counter", "last_comment_created": 1791916467654, "content": "<ol start=\"800\">\n<li>\n<ol start=\"500\">\n<li>\n<ol start=\"450\">\n<li></li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The numbers that would make your pellet rifle a federal &quot;firearm.&quot;</p>\n<p>A lot of kids learn to shoot with a pellet rifle, plinking cans in the backyard or keeping squirrels off the bird feeder, long before they ever carry a .22 into the woods. A California politician wants Congress to put that pellet rifle under federal gun control.</p>\n<p>The bill is H.R. 10583, filed September 24th by Rep. Kevin Mullin (D-CA-15), and its title says it's written &quot;to classify lethal air guns as firearms.&quot; Once an air gun counts as a &quot;firearm&quot; under the federal Gun Control Act, buying one from a store means a federal background check, and the gun gets a serial number. The companies that make them and the stores that sell them need federal firearms licenses, and dealers keep federal paperwork on every sale.</p>\n<p>==\nWhat counts as a &quot;lethal air gun&quot;</p>\n<p>.177 caliber pellet\n800 feet per second or faster</p>\n<p>.22 caliber pellet\n500 feet per second or faster</p>\n<p>.25 caliber pellet\n450 feet per second or faster</p>\n<p>Metallic pellet above .25 caliber\nAny speed at all</p>\n<h1>And then\nAny other air gun the Attorney General designates, through rulemaking, as &quot;capable of causing death&quot;</h1>\n<p>Any gun that can hit those numbers is a &quot;lethal air gun&quot; under the bill. The only ones carved out fire nothing but paint-filled pellets. That covers most serious pellet rifles sold today.</p>\n<p>Now look at that last line. The bill lets the Attorney General add more air guns through rulemaking, any he decides are &quot;capable of causing death,&quot; and it puts no limit on what that means. Today it's 800 feet per second. The bill already gives the Attorney General a blank check to decide which air guns come next.</p>\n<p>The Red Ryder isn't on the list today. Daisy rates it at up to 350 feet per second, well under the line. But the bill lets the Attorney General add any air gun he deems &quot;capable of causing death.&quot;</p>\n<p>Add your name to the North Carolina Firearms Coalition petition against H.R. 10583.\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://action.ncfirearmscoalition.org/hr10583_pet?e=700b3d0d28cf25a534ef5a5f6eaf0d4b&amp;utm_source=ncfc&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=20261013_bbgun_rm2&amp;n=3\" target=\"_blank\">https://action.ncfirearmscoalition.org/hr10583_pet?e=700b3d0d28cf25a534ef5a5f6eaf0d4b&amp;utm_source=ncfc&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=20261013_bbgun_rm2&amp;n=3</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 13, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVeu8AAU", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 779, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8882902, "raw_content": "", "author": "CleanUpPhillyTrump24", "created": 1791830318914, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "MacheteSanta", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVeu8AAU.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/TwH1Cs1o3tW7.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/MaBcXEsZvMcMuQAq.jpeg", "width":